gy, but the\ndocs-authoring priority exception derives the docs epic's priority from the\nstrategy frontmatter (`priority: Major` → P1). The exception also means E004\ndoes not push P1 upstream to the implementations it depends on.\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\n- All epic `component` values are copied verbatim from\n  `.context/rhai-components.txt`: `Dashboard`, `Model Registry`,\n  `Documentation`.\n- **Data Science Pipelines is passive.** It is listed as affected but needs no\n  code changes — run parameters and metrics are already exposed through the\n  existing per-run surfaces the Dashboard reads. Validation (comparison\n  renders parameters and metrics correctly for pipeline runs and training\n  runs) is an acceptance criterion on E001, the nearest active component's\n  epic, validated by the same (Dashboard) team — no separate validation epic\n  is warranted.\n- HLR-2 spans two components: the lineage representation on model versions\n  (Model Registry backend, E002) and the user-facing entry point (the\n  registry UI lives in the Dashboard per architecture context, E003). This is\n  an architectural split along component/team boundaries, not a priority\n  split.\n- Teams were derived from the architecture-context owning-team fields\n  (`RHOAI Dashboard`, `Model Registry`) because the strategy lists no teams.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): Affected Components is a bare\n  list with no change descriptions or owner teams; there is no Impacted Teams\n  table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n  non-functional requirements. Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the\n  HLRs; teams were derived from architecture context.\n- **Docs epic ownership assumption:** the strategy names no documentation\n  owner. E004 is assigned to the RHOAI Dashboard team as owner of the primary\n  documented surface; confirm the owner before implementation.\n- **\"Training runs\" source unspecified:** 