{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-456f6ea1-03d4-4609-aee9-8ab0c9099c46","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2847ea98d862554","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-v42z7xap/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Dashboard run comparison view for training and pipeline runs\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the run comparison capability in the Dashboard: users select two or\nmore training or pipeline runs and view their parameters and metrics side by\nside, including a diff presentation that highlights which parameters and\nmetrics changed between two selected runs. This replaces the current\nspreadsheet-export workflow for comparing candidate runs during model\npromotion decisions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Multi-select of runs from the Dashboard runs list (both training runs and\n  pipeline runs).\n- Side-by-side view of parameters and metrics for the selected runs.\n- Diff presentation mode for a comparison of exactly two runs, highlighting\n  the parameters and metrics whose values differ.\n- The comparison reads run parameters and metrics from the run data the\n  Dashboard already surfaces; Data Science Pipelines requires no code changes\n  for this and is validated through the acceptance criteria below.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given two or more runs selected from the runs list, When the user opens the\n  comparison, Then the parameters and metrics of every selected run are\n  displayed side by side in a single Dashboard view.\n- Given exactly two runs in the comparison, When the diff presentation is\n  enabled, Then parameters and metrics whose values differ between the two\n  runs are highlighted and distinguishable from unchanged ones.\n- Given both pipeline runs and training runs exist in a project, When runs of\n  either kind are selected for comparison, Then the same comparison surface\n  renders their parameters and metrics correctly (passive validation of Data\n  Science Pipelines — no changes to that component).\n- Given a selected run with no recorded parameters or metrics, When it is\n  compared, Then the comparison renders without errors and marks the missing\n  values.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and\n  metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n- HLR-3 (P1): a run diff view highlighting which parameters and metrics\n  changed between two selected runs. HLR-3 is a presentation mode of the same\n  comparison surface over the same run data as HLR-1, so both requirements are\n  covered by this epic at the higher priority (P0).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32107,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8534e1ce304e7260","agent_id":"a6379c6e1d835bb29","session_id":"bfa11520-8a30-46f6-a648-bb273d1f61ab","uuid":"bc1a781a-b998-4ec8-ab5f-5e514ff2b25a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:42:26.452Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
