{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-45a325fb-e4c8-41d5-9e97-1a89bb20e1a6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8541035521d6002b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-v42z7xap/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Run lineage on registered model versions\n\n## Description\n\nEstablishes, in the Model Registry, a resolvable link from a registered model\nversion back to the run (training or pipeline) that produced it, so that\nplatform surfaces can resolve and compare the run behind a registered model.\nThis is the registry-side foundation for opening a run comparison from the\nModel Registry.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Represent the producing run on registered model versions, using the existing\n  custom-properties extension point on ModelVersion entities as the\n  architecture-defined mechanism for attaching structured metadata.\n- Expose the lineage through the Model Registry REST API so the Dashboard can\n  resolve the run behind a model version.\n- Define behavior for model versions registered without run linkage: the\n  absent lineage must not break registry operations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a model version registered from a run, When the version is retrieved\n  through the Model Registry REST API, Then it carries a resolvable reference\n  to the run that produced it.\n- Given a model version with no producing run recorded, When the version is\n  retrieved, Then the missing lineage is represented cleanly and registry\n  operations continue to work.\n- Given the lineage reference is read by a consumer, Then it is sufficient to\n  identify the run in the Dashboard (project and run identity).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n  them (registry backend portion of the requirement).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_s