{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a327187ef275948","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\ttitle: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Major\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\tlinks: []\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Problem Statement\n12\t\n13\tData scientists iterate across dozens of training and pipeline runs but have no\n14\tway to compare them inside the platform: parameters and metrics live in\n15\tper-run pages, so comparison happens in exported spreadsheets. Model promotion\n16\tdecisions need side-by-side visibility into what changed between candidate\n17\truns and how their metrics differ. (Requirements below were consolidated from\n18\ttwo customer councils; some overlap in wording was kept from the sources.)\n19\t\n20\t## High-Level Requirements\n21\t\n22\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n23\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n24\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and metrics side by side in the Dashboard. |\n25\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Registered model versions link back to the run that produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry. |\n26\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Provide a run \"diff\" view that highlights which parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs. |\n27\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers the comparison workflow from both the runs list and the registry. |\n28\t\n29\t## Affected Components\n30\t\n31\t- Dashboard\n32\t- Model Registry\n33\t- Data Science Pipelines\n34\t\n35\t## Out of Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Automatic best-run selection or promotion\n38\t- Comparison across clusters or across projects\n39\t\n40\t## Open Questions\n41\t\n42\tNone.\n43\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8818204d23847bbb","agent_id":"acafebda25c761247","session_id":"bfa11520-8a30-46f6-a648-bb273d1f61ab","uuid":"a24cce98-e10e-48b8-893f-d6b906713fd4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:48:59.2