{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba53833eb4634b65","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n11\t\n12\tTriage: full decomposition (not below-threshold — the strategy spans three\n13\tcomponents and multiple teams, and mixes Dashboard/Model Registry code\n14\timplementation with substantive documentation authoring; not docs-only — code\n15\tchanges are required in Dashboard and Model Registry).\n16\t\n17\t## Epic List\n18\t\n19\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n20\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n21\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Dashboard run comparison view for training and pipeline runs | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Run lineage on registered model versions | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open run comparison from the Model Registry | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Documentation for the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n25\t\n26\t## Dependency DAG\n27\t\n28\t```mermaid\n29\tgraph TD\n30\t    E001[\"E001 Dashboard run comparison view (P0)\"] --> E003[\"E003 Open comparison from Model Registry (P1)\"]\n31\t    E002[\"E002 Run lineage on model versions (P1)\"] --> E003\n32\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 Comparison workflow docs (P1)\"]\n33\t    E002 --> E004\n34\t    E003 --> E004\n35\t```\n36\t\n37\tE001 and E002 are roots and run in parallel (different components, different\n38\trepos, no shared artifacts). Critical path length: 3 (E001 → E003 → E004, or\n39\tE002 → E003 → E004).\n40\t\n41\t## DAG Justification\n42\t\n43\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n44\t|------|------|-----------|\n45\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The registry entry point navigates into the run comparison view; the consuming Dashboard work builds against the comparison surface produced by the comparison epic. |\n46\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The registry entry point resolves the producing run through the Model Registry REST API lineage surface; it is an API the consumer builds against, not a configuration reference. |\n47\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the implemented comparison workflow. |\n48\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the registry-side lineage workflow. |\n49\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes opening a comparison from the registry. |\n50\t| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 14 (parallel) | Different components and repos with no shared artifacts; the P0 comparison work must not be gated by the P1 registry lineage work. |\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n53\t\n54\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n55\t|-----|----------|---------|\n56\t| HLR-1 — select two or more runs, view parameters and metrics side by side | P0 | E001 |\n57\t| HLR-2 — registered model versions link back to the producing run; comparison openable from the Model Registry | P1 | E002 (registry backend), E003 (Dashboard entry point) |\n58\t| HLR-3 — run diff view highlighting changed parameters and metrics | P1 | E001 (consolidated with HLR-1) |\n59\t| HLR-4 — documentation covers the comparison workflow | P2 | E004 |\n60\t\n61\tAll HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n62\t\n63\t**HLR consolidation note (HLR-1 + HLR-3):** HLR-3's diff view is a\n64\tpresentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data as\n65\tHLR-1 — the strategy itself notes the requirements were consolidated from two\n66\tcustomer councils with overlapping wording kept. Per the redundant-HLR rule\n67\tthey are ONE capability covered by a single epic (E001) at the higher priority\n68\t(P0). Splitting them would produce two epics building the same surface plus an\n69\tartificial serialization edge.\n70\t\n71\t**Priority note on E004:** HLR-4 is P2 in the strategy, but the\n72\tdocs-authoring priority exception derives the docs epic's priority from the\n73\tstrategy frontmatter (`priority: Major` → P1). The exception also means E004\n74\tdoes not push P1 upstream to the implementations it depends on.\n75\t\n76\t## Component Mapping Notes\n77\t\n78\t- All epic `component` values are copied verbatim from\n79\t  `.context/rhai-components.txt`: `Dashboard`, `Model Registry`,\n80\t  `Documentation`.\n81\t- **Data Science Pipelines is passive.** It is listed as affected but needs no\n82\t  code changes — run parameters and metrics are already exposed through the\n83\t  existing per-run surfaces the Dashboard reads. Validation (comparison\n84\t  renders parameters and metrics correctly for pipeline runs and training\n85\t  runs) is an acceptance criterion on E001, the nearest active component's\n86\t  epic, validated by the same (Dashboard) team — no separate validation epic\n87\t  is warranted.\n88\t- HLR-2 spans two components: the lineage representation on model versions\n89\t  (Model Registry backend, E002) and the user-facing entry point (the\n90\t  registry UI lives in the Dashboard per architecture context, E003). This is\n91\t  an architectural split along component/team boundaries, not a priority\n92\t  split.\n93\t- Teams were derived from the architecture-context owning-team fields\n94\t  (`RHOAI Dashboard`, `Model Registry`) because the strategy lists no teams.\n95\t\n96\t## Health Warnings\n97\t\n98\t- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): Affected Components is a bare\n99\t  list with no change descriptions or owner teams; there is no Impacted Teams\n100\t  table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n101\t  non-functional requirements. Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the\n102\t  HLRs; teams were derived from architecture context.\n103\t- **Docs epic ownership assumption:** the strategy names no documentation\n104\t  owner. E004 is assigned to the RHOAI Dashboard team as owner of the primary\n105\t  documented surface; confirm the owner before implementation.\n106\t- **\"Training runs\" source unspecified:** the title and problem statement\n107\t  reference training runs, but Training Operator is not among the affected\n108\t  components. E001 treats run kinds as whatever the Dashboard's existing run\n109\t  surfaces expose and carries an AC covering both pipeline and training runs;\n110\t  if training-run metadata turns out to be inaccessible, that is a fix-and-\n111\t  retry implementation matter (no open question in the strategy suggests a\n112\t  different epic structure).\n113\t- **Priority observation:** HLR-4 is P2 in the strategy while the docs epic\n114\t  carries P1 — this is the docs-authoring priority exception (Major → P1), not\n115\t  an inversion.\n116\t\n117\t## Tiered Delivery\n118\t\n119\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\n120\tin-platform.\n121\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8818204d23847bbb","agent_id":"acafebda25c761247","session_id":"bfa11520-8a30-46f6-a648-bb273d1f61ab","uuid":"99e7222b-584f-49c9-96e5-eb1b6fe41c9b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:49:00.137Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba53833eb4634b65","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
