{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a37f45e7742cbb1c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Run lineage on registered model versions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run lineage on registered model versions\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tEstablishes, in the Model Registry, a resolvable link from a registered model\n34\tversion back to the run (training or pipeline) that produced it, so that\n35\tplatform surfaces can resolve and compare the run behind a registered model.\n36\tThis is the registry-side foundation for opening a run comparison from the\n37\tModel Registry.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Represent the producing run on registered model versions, using the existing\n42\t  custom-properties extension point on ModelVersion entities as the\n43\t  architecture-defined mechanism for attaching structured metadata.\n44\t- Expose the lineage through the Model Registry REST API so the Dashboard can\n45\t  resolve the run behind a model version.\n46\t- Define behavior for model versions registered without run linkage: the\n47\t  absent lineage must not break registry operations.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given a model version registered from a run, When the version is retrieved\n52\t  through the Model Registry REST API, Then it carries a re